        "content": "{\"formal\": {\"statement\": \"open Filter Topology Metric in\\n∀ p : Polynomial ℝ, ∃ C : ℝ, p.degree = 1999 → ‖p.eval 0‖ ≤ C * ∫ x in (-1)..1, ‖p.eval x‖\", \"namespace\": \"\", \"supporting_declarations\": [], \"rendered\": \"∀ (p : (Polynomial ℝ)),\\n  (∃ C, ((p.degree = 1999) → (‖(Polynomial.eval 0 p)‖ ≤ (C * (∫ (x : ℝ) in (-1)..1, ‖(Polynomial.eval x p)‖)))))\"}, \"signature\": \": ∀ p : Polynomial ℝ, ∃ C : ℝ, p.degree = 1999 → ‖p.eval 0‖ ≤ C * ∫ x in (-1)..1, ‖p.eval x‖\", \"informal\": \"Prove that there is a constant $C$ such that, if $p(x)$ is a polynomial of degree 1999, then \\\\[|p(0)|\\\\leq C \\\\int_{-1}^1 |p(x)|\\\\,dx.\\\\]\", \"docstring\": \"/--\\nProve that there is a constant $C$ such that, if $p(x)$ is a polynomial of degree 1999, then \\\\[|p(0)|\\\\leq C \\\\int_{-1}^1 |p(x)|\\\\,dx.\\\\]\\n-/\", \"prechecks\": {\"status\": \"completed\", \"hints\": [], \"vacuity\": \"unresolved\"}, \"advisory\": {\"paraphrase_status\": \"completed\", \"differences\": [\"The paraphrase is more general, mentioning all polynomials with real coefficients, while the informal version is more specific about the degree being 1999.\", \"The condition in the paraphrase is explicit, while the informal version does not specify the degree.\", \"The paraphrase explicitly mentions the constant C, while the informal version refers to it as a constant without specifying.\", \"The inequality in the paraphrase is written with absolute values, while the informal version uses |p(0)| ≤ C ∫|p(x)|dx.\", \"The paraphrase includes a note about the source and model being untrusted data, which is not present in the informal version.\"], \"paraphrase\": \"For every polynomial p with real coefficients, there exists a real number C such that if the degree of p is 1999, then the absolute value of p evaluated at 0 is less than or equal to C multiplied by the integral of the absolute value of p evaluated at x from -1 to 1.\", \"comparison_status\": \"completed\"}}"
